      "body": "## Motivation\n\nExpert output encoding creates temporary byte buffers before it returns a base64 string.\nThis change removes those buffers in the detokenizer and tokenizer fallback.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Encode contiguous NumPy buffers directly into base64 strings.\n- Preserve C-order bytes for non-contiguous tensors.\n- Keep missing items and pre-encoded strings unchanged.\n\nThis PR changes no IPC socket behavior.\nThe optional MessagePack socket optimization is separate in https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/45097.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nLocal CPU tests passed:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python python -m pytest -q \\\n  test/registered/unit/managers/test_output_serialization.py \\\n  test/registered/unit/managers/test_tokenizer_manager_rid_cleanup.py\n# 50 passed\n```\n\nThe tests check byte equality, non-contiguous tensors, empty tensors, missing items, and pre-encoded strings.\nBoth routed experts and indexer output use the same encoding checks.\n\n`isort --check-only`, `ruff format --check`, `ruff check --select F401,F821,F823,UP037`, and `git diff --check` passed for the changed files.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n| CPU operation | Payload | Before | After | Change |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Base64 encoding | 6 MiB tensor → 8 MiB string | 1.420 ms | 0.489 ms | -65.6% |\n\nThe encoding gain applies to both pickle and MessagePack IPC.\nThe measured encoding code stays the same after the PR split.\nThe benchmark uses thread CPU time and three interleaved runs, with five batches per run.\nThe host uses an Intel Xeon Platinum 8568Y+, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.14.1 CPU, and pybase64 1.5.1.\nThese results measure CPU cost, not model throughput.\nNo GPU serving benchmark ran.\n\nCompanion Dynamo draft PR: https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/16765.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Add CPU regression tests.\n- [x] Run local tests and formatting checks.\n- [x] Record CPU performance measurements.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39200316964](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39200316964)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39200316825](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39200316825)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39200317070](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39200317070)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n",
